  (13
  ("T" 0.1177 0.1651 0.2481 0.3044 0.3044 0.0563 nil nil 0.0474 "AAAAAC+LiberationSans" 0.0600 nil nil 0)
  ("preface" 0.4188 0.5803 0.1581 0.1922 0.1922 0.0341 nil 0.2361 0.1615 "AAAAAC+LiberationSans" 0.0364 nil nil 0)
  ("his book can make a profound difference in how you look at and" 0.1682 0.7929 0.2574 0.2739 0.2739 0.0165 0.00588 0.2880 0.0280 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("understand learning. You will learn the simplest, most effective, and most" 0.1682 0.8665 0.2792 0.2958 0.2958 0.0165 0.00588 0.3082 0.1047 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("efficient techniques researchers know about how to learn. And you’ll have fun" 0.1177 0.8694 0.3010 0.3176 0.3176 0.0165 0.00588 0.2838 0.0783 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("while you’re doing it." 0.1177 0.3282 0.3229 0.3394 0.3394 0.0165 0.00588 0.3075 0.0528 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("What’s surprising is that a lot of learners use ineffective and inefficient" 0.1577 0.8442 0.3447 0.3612 0.3612 0.0165 0.00588 0.2996 0.0668 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("strategies. In my laboratory, for example, we have surveyed college students" 0.1177 0.8539 0.3665 0.3830 0.3830 0.0165 0.00588 0.3075 0.0977 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("about their learning. They most commonly use the strategy of repeated reading" 0.1177 0.8800 0.3883 0.4048 0.4048 0.0165 0.00588 0.3205 0.0536 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("—simply reading through books or notes over and over. We and other" 0.1177 0.7949 0.4101 0.4266 0.4266 0.0165 0.00588 0.3395 0.0894 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("researchers have found that this passive and shallow strategy often produces" 0.1177 0.8515 0.4320 0.4485 0.4485 0.0165 0.00588 0.2548 0.1115 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("minimal or no learning. We call this “labor in vain”—students are putting in" 0.1177 0.8518 0.4538 0.4703 0.4703 0.0165 0.00588 0.3703 0.0807 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("labor but not getting anywhere." 0.1177 0.4188 0.4756 0.4921 0.4921 0.0165 0.00588 0.2968 0.0502 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("We don’t engage in passive rereading because we are dumb or lazy. We do" 0.1577 0.8753 0.4974 0.5139 0.5139 0.0165 0.00588 0.3177 0.0305 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("it because we fall prey to a cognitive illusion. When we read material over and" 0.1177 0.8753 0.5192 0.5357 0.5357 0.0165 0.00588 0.3397 0.0136 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("over, the material becomes familiar and fluent, meaning it is easy for our" 0.1177 0.8231 0.5410 0.5576 0.5576 0.0165 0.00588 0.3415 0.0494 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("minds to process. We then think that this easy processing is a sign that we have" 0.1177 0.8716 0.5628 0.5794 0.5794 0.0165 0.00588 0.3310 0.0586 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("learned something well, even though we have not." 0.1177 0.5988 0.5847 0.6012 0.6012 0.0165 0.00588 0.3117 0.0718 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("This book will introduce you to this and other illusions of learning and" 0.1577 0.8447 0.6065 0.6230 0.6230 0.0165 0.00588 0.2971 0.0433 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("give you tools to overcome them. And it will introduce great new tools, such" 0.1177 0.8577 0.6283 0.6448 0.6448 0.0165 0.00588 0.3501 0.0422 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("as retrieval practice, that can have a powerful effect in boosting the “bang for" 0.1177 0.8619 0.6501 0.6666 0.6666 0.0165 0.00588 0.2781 0.0197 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("your buck” from your time spent in learning. It’s a deeply practical yet" 0.1177 0.7983 0.6720 0.6885 0.6885 0.0165 0.00588 0.3094 0.0443 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("inspiring book that helps you see clearly why some approaches are so much" 0.1177 0.8518 0.6938 0.7103 0.7103 0.0165 0.00588 0.2899 0.0871 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("more effective than others." 0.1177 0.3765 0.7156 0.7321 0.7321 0.0165 0.00588 0.3029 0.0516 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("We’re on the edge of an explosion in knowledge about how to learn most" 0.1577 0.8654 0.7374 0.7539 0.7539 0.0165 0.00588 0.3196 0.0587 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("effectively. In this new world of insight, you’ll find A Mind for Numbers to be" 0.1177 0.8646 0.7592 0.7758 0.7758 0.0165 0.00588 0.3427 0.1071 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("an indispensable guide." 0.1177 0.3423 0.7810 0.7976 0.7976 0.0165 0.00588 0.2190 0.0223 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("—Jeffrey D. Karpicke, James V. Bradley Associate Professor of Psychological" 0.1400 0.8818 0.8319 0.8485 0.8485 0.0165 0.00588 0.2998 0.0857 "AAAAAB+LiberationSerif-Italic" 0.0182 nil t 0)
  ("Sciences, Purdue University" 0.6141 0.8822 0.8538 0.8703 0.8703 0.0165 0.00588 0.2575 0.0882 "AAAAAB+LiberationSerif-Italic" 0.0182 nil t 0))
