  ("engineering." 0.1177 0.2400 0.3883 0.4048 0.4048 0.0165 nil 0.1835 0.1224 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("Growing up, I hated math and science. I flunked my way through high" 0.1577 0.8318 0.4101 0.4266 0.4266 0.0165 0.00588 0.3367 0.0871 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("school math and science courses, and only started studying trigonometry—" 0.1177 0.8435 0.4320 0.4485 0.4485 0.0165 0.00588 0.2938 0.0642 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("remedial trigonometry—when I was twenty-six years old." 0.1177 0.6741 0.4538 0.4703 0.4703 0.0165 0.00588 0.3626 0.0854 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("As a youngster, even the simple concept of reading a clock face didn’t" 0.1577 0.8336 0.4756 0.4921 0.4921 0.0165 0.00588 0.2901 0.0256 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("seem to make sense to me. Why should the little hand point toward the hour?" 0.1177 0.8540 0.4974 0.5139 0.5139 0.0165 0.00588 0.3711 0.0489 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("Shouldn’t it be the big hand, since the hour was more important than the" 0.1177 0.8093 0.5192 0.5357 0.5357 0.0165 0.00588 0.3323 0.0948 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("minute? Did the clock read ten ten? Or one fifty? I was perpetually confused." 0.1177 0.8553 0.5410 0.5576 0.5576 0.0165 0.00588 0.3126 0.0763 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("Worse than my problems with clocks was the television. In those days before" 0.1177 0.8563 0.5628 0.5794 0.5794 0.0165 0.00588 0.3390 0.0622 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("the remote control, I didn’t even know which button turned the television on. I" 0.1177 0.8667 0.5847 0.6012 0.6012 0.0165 0.00588 0.3274 0.0281 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("watched a show only in the company of my brother or sister. They not only" 0.1177 0.8424 0.6065 0.6230 0.6230 0.0165 0.00588 0.3336 0.0776 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("could turn the TV on, but could also tune the channel to the program we wanted" 0.1177 0.8823 0.6283 0.6448 0.6448 0.0165 0.00588 0.3286 0.0541 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("to watch. Nice." 0.1177 0.2588 0.6501 0.6666 0.6666 0.0165 0.00588 0.3909 0.0176 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("All I could conclude, looking at my technical ineptitude and flunking" 0.1577 0.8200 0.6720 0.6885 0.6885 0.0165 0.00588 0.3070 0.0301 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("grades in math and science, was that I wasn’t very smart. At least, not that way. I" 0.1177 0.8820 0.6938 0.7103 0.7103 0.0165 0.00588 0.3604 0.0644 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("didn’t realize it then, but my self-portrait as being technically, scientifically," 0.1177 0.8471 0.7156 0.7321 0.7321 0.0165 0.00588 0.2881 0.0571 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("and mathematically incapable was shaping my life. At the root of it all was my" 0.1177 0.8706 0.7374 0.7539 0.7539 0.0165 0.00588 0.3694 0.0341 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("problem with mathematics. I had come to think of numbers and equations as" 0.1177 0.8480 0.7592 0.7758 0.7758 0.0165 0.00588 0.3572 0.0818 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("akin to one of life’s deadly diseases—to be avoided at all costs. I didn’t realize" 0.1177 0.8728 0.7810 0.7976 0.7976 0.0165 0.00588 0.3212 0.0412 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("then that there were simple mental tricks that could have brought math into" 0.1177 0.8341 0.8028 0.8194 0.8194 0.0165 0.00588 0.3424 0.0400 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
  ("focus for me, tricks that are helpful not only for people who are bad at math," 0.1177 0.8565 0.8247 0.8412 0.8412 0.0165 0.00588 0.3219 0.0527 "AAAAAA+LiberationSerif" 0.0182 nil nil 0)
